{"type":"npc","name":"Invulnerabug","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":220,"temp":0,"max":220,"details":""},"ac":{"value":42,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":35,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"burrow","value":35},{"type":"fly","value":20}],"details":"relentless tunneler"},"immunities":[{"type":"death-effects","exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["chthonian","common","diabolic","empyrean"],"details":""},"level":{"value":16},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Roaches and rats are the bane of mortal homeowners, yet these nuisances are welcome guests compared to invulnerabugs. Invulnerabugs are the pests that demigods and other powerful planar beings worry about invading their homes. These insects infest celestial castles and fiendish fortresses alike.</p><p>With their adamantine mandibles, invulnerabugs can and will chew through any substance, though they prefer to eat rare and precious materials. Their magically enhanced carapaces offer them versatile defenses against a wide range of threats.</p><p>While invulnerabugs are merely a pest for demigods, when an invulnerabug invades a mortal's home, it's best to just move and let the bug win.</p><h2>Eye of the Beholder</h2><p>Invulnerabugs form large, eusocial colonies, with each member belonging to a caste that determines their roles and responsibilities, such as raising children, defending the colony, or planning new construction. They use their knowledge of architecture to draw artful tunnels and avoid compromising the structural integrity of the buildings they infest, but few people enjoy living in buildings that are riddled with tiny holes. Invulnerabugs take offense to anyone who insults their destructive art or attempts to drive them away, but they can make stalwart allies to those who compliment their work and provide plenty of rare materials to eat.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 1,250/2,800/5,150 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing), armor (heavy), shield, perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Lore [Architecture], Religion, Stealth, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> acid, body, bane, constitution, dexterity, energy resistant (acid, cold, electricity, fire, force, sonic, spirit, vitality, void), fortification, metal, sensory (darkvision, scent), spells (Divine: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.UG0SmRYSdbrx2rTA]{Indestructibility}), strength, sturdy, throwing, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"David Greene","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":8},"dex":{"mod":6},"con":{"mod":6},"int":{"mod":4},"wis":{"mod":5},"cha":{"mod":2}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":25,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"scent","acuity":"imprecise","range":60}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":30,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":28,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":25,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":26},"athletics":{"base":30},"religion":{"base":28},"stealth":{"base":32},"survival":{"base":27}},"traits":{"value":["beast"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"tiny"}}},"_id":"XHQyGD12H4GPyKZy","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/invulnerabug.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Invulnerabug","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":0.5,"height":0.5,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/invulnerabug.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2"